course: dictionary
lesson: 12710
title: Dominican: a name with a capital letter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dominican starts with a capital D because it is a name. It tells us where a person or thing is from, or what group they belong to. «Ana is Dominican, and her family comes from the Dominican Republic.» Here Dominican tells us where Ana's family is from.
explain: Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. «The Dominican friar read quietly in the old church.» A friar is a religious man, and church is a clue, so this Dominican means a member of a religious order, not a person from a country.
explain: Dominica and the Dominican Republic are two different places, so read carefully. «Our class read about Dominica, a small island country in the Caribbean.» Dominica is the small island. The Dominican Republic is the country that shares an island with Haiti.
fact: Dominican is a name, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Dominican can mean from or connected with the Dominican Republic, or from Dominica.
fact: The Dominican Republic is a country in the Caribbean that shares an island with Haiti.
fact: Dominica is a small, different island country in the Caribbean.
fact: A Dominican friar or nun belongs to the Dominican Order, a Catholic religious order started by Saint Dominic in the 1200s.
exercise: «Maria is Dominican, and her family comes from the Dominican Republic.» Where does the word Dominican point? | A sunny day at the beach | A friar in a church | *From or connected with the Dominican Republic | A very old castle
exercise: «The Dominican friar read quietly in the old church.» What is a Dominican friar? | A kind of Caribbean weather | *A friar or nun of the Dominican Order | A person who sells fish at the market | A teacher at a school
exercise: Why does Dominican start with a capital D? | Because it is a very long word | *Because it is a name of a people, a place or a group | Because it is always the first word in a sentence | Because it is written in red on the page
test: «Dominica is a small island country in the Caribbean.» Which country is Dominica? | *A small island country in the Caribbean | A kind of church bell | A river in Africa | A large country in Europe
test: «Saint Dominic started the Dominican Order in the 1200s.» Who started the Dominican Order? | A Scottish farmer | Grandad | *Saint Dominic | Haiti
exam: Dominica and the Dominican Republic are different places. Which statement is true? | Dominica is the larger of the two | Both of them are in Europe | *The Dominican Republic shares an island with Haiti, and Dominica is a small island country | They are the same place
